  "verification_evidence": "The M9 medium (pH = 7-7.5) consisted of 11 g/L of 5x M9 salts (Sigma Aldrich, St. Louis, MO), 2 mM MgSO4.7H2O, 0.1 mM CaCl2.2H2O, 1 mg/L of Thiamine HCl, 3 mg/L of FeSO4.7H2O, and trace minerals. [Carbon] 10 g/L glucose. [Selection] Chloramphenicol 30 mg/L. 'All cultivations were aerobic and conducted in 5 mL cultures in test tubes on a rotary shaker at 250 rpm at 37 C.'",
